    "summary": "Master the distinction between workflows and chains, explore parallel fan-out, and learn how to implement sequential pipelines and conditional router nodes.",
    "content": "### 1. What are LLM Chains? (The Definitive Definition)\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Formal Technical Definition (Exam Standard):**  \n> An **LLM Chain** is a deterministic, sequential software composition pattern in AI engineering where two or more distinct computational units (such as prompt templates, language models, external tools, or output parsers) are linked together in a fixed series, such that the processed output of step $N$ serves as the direct typed input to step $N+1$.\n\n> [!TIP]\n> **\ud83d\udca1 In Simple Words:**  \n> An LLM Chain is like a relay race where runners pass a baton. Runner 1 (Prompt Template) formats the question and hands it to Runner 2 (LLM). Runner 2 generates text and hands it to Runner 3 (JSON Parser). Runner 3 parses it into clean data. If anyone drops the baton, the chain stops.\n\n```text\nTHE 4 CORE EXECUTION TOPOLOGIES\n1. Sequential (Linear Pipeline):\n   [ Input ] \u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Prompt Template ] \u2500\u2500\u25ba [ LLM Generation ] \u2500\u2500\u25ba [ JSON Parser ] \u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Output ]\n\n2. Parallel Fan-Out / Fan-In:\n                 \u250c\u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Worker 1: Legal Risk Analysis ] \u2500\u2500\u2510\n   [ Contract ] \u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Worker 2: Financial Liability ] \u2500\u2500\u253c\u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Aggregator LLM ] \u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Final Audit ]\n                 \u2514\u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Worker 3: SLA Verification     ] \u2500\u2500\u2518\n\n3. Conditional Router:\n                 \u250c\u2500\u2500 [ Intent == \"Refund\" ] \u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Process Refund Node ]\n   [ Query ] \u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Classifier LLM ]\n                 \u2514\u2500\u2500 [ Intent == \"Tech\"   ] \u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Diagnostic Node    ]\n\n4. Evaluator-Optimizer (Self-Reflective Loop):\n   \u250c\u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Generator LLM: Draft Code ] \u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Unit Test Sandbox / Critic LLM ] \u2500\u2500\u2510\n   \u2502                                                 \u2502 (Fails Tests)           \u2502 (Passes)\n   \u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500 [ Error Trace & Critique ] \u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u25ba [ Production Deploy ]\n```\n\n---\n\n### 2. Deep Dive: Sequential vs. Conditional Execution\n\n#### 1. Sequential Chaining (LCEL Pipes)\nSequential pipelines are ideal for deterministic data transformation where the path never changes:\n\n```python\nfrom langchain_core.prompts import ChatPromptTemplate\nfrom langchain_core.output_parsers import StrOutputParser\nfrom langchain_openai import ChatOpenAI\n\nllm = ChatOpenAI(model=\"gpt-4o-mini\", temperature=0)\n\n# Step 1: Summarize\nsummary_prompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_template(\"Summarize this document in 3 bullet points:\n\n{text}\")\n\n# Step 2: Translate\ntranslate_prompt = ChatPromptTemplate.from_template(\"Translate this summary to Khmer:\n\n{summary}\")\n\n# LCEL Pipeline Composition\nchain = (\n    summary_prompt \n    | llm \n    | StrOutputParser() \n    | (lambda summary: {\"summary\": summary}) \n    | translate_prompt \n    | llm \n    | StrOutputParser()\n)\n\nresult = chain.invoke({\"text\": \"Cambodia is accelerating its national AI strategy...\"})\n```\n\n#### 2. Conditional Routing (Classification Before Action)\n\n> [!IMPORTANT]\n> **High-Yield Exam Concept:** Why must router nodes classify intent into strict enums or schemas before dispatching tools?\n> * **Zero Hallucination Routing:** If an LLM is allowed to generate arbitrary text during routing, downstream nodes receive invalid function arguments.\n> * **Cost & Latency Optimization:** By routing a simple FAQ query to a fast, cheap model or cache, you avoid invoking expensive multi-agent reasoning chains unnecessarily.\n\n---\n\n### High-Yield Exam Takeaways\n\n* **Composition Law:** In LangChain LCEL, the pipe operator `|` creates a `RunnableSequence`. Every component must implement the `Runnable` interface (`invoke`, `batch`, `stream`).\n* **Router Determinism:** Always constrain routing classifiers using strict schemas (e.g. `Literal[\"billing\", \"tech_support\", \"sales\"]`) rather than free-form text.\n* **Parallel Execution Speedup:** In parallel fan-out patterns (e.g., analyzing 3 sections of a document simultaneously), total latency equals $\\max(t_1, t_2, t_3)$, not $t_1 + t_2 + t_3$."
